meta {
  name: Update Bug Report
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/bug-reports/{{bugReportId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "triaged",
    "internalNotes": "Reproduced. The leaderboard query caches per month and the sold write does not invalidate it."
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("applies both fields and stamps who moved it", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.status).to.equal("triaged");
    expect(body.internalNotes).to.contain("Reproduced");
    expect(body.statusUpdatedAt).to.not.equal(null);
    expect(body.statusUpdatedByName).to.not.equal(null);
  });

  test("returns the full detail, so the sheet needs no refetch", function () {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.have.property("description");
    expect(res.getBody()).to.have.property("context");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /platform/bug-reports/:id — triage

  Sets the status and/or the internal notes. Returns the **full detail**, the
  same shape as `GET :id`, so the detail sheet updates from the response rather
  than refetching.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `platform:bugs:write`
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`)

  ⚠ Note the split from the two reads above, which need only
  `platform:bugs:read`. Every platform admin holds both
  (`ALL_PLATFORM_PERMISSIONS`), so it only bites if the permission is ever
  narrowed — but the page gates on `read` and this endpoint on `write`, so a
  read-only holder would reach `/admin/bugs` and be refused on save.

  ## Body
  | field         | type   | notes                                              |
  |---------------|--------|-----------------------------------------------------|
  | status        | enum   | `new` \| `triaged` \| `in_progress` \| `resolved` \| `wont_fix` |
  | internalNotes | string | ≤ 5,000 chars. **`""` clears the note**; omitting the field leaves it alone. |

  Both optional, **at least one required** — a PATCH that says nothing is a
  client bug, and returning the unchanged record would hide it.

  ## Not a state machine

  Any status is reachable from any other. A queue that argues with the person
  working it gets worked around rather than used.

  ## `statusUpdatedBy` / `statusUpdatedAt` move only on a real status change

  Editing a note is not a triage decision. Stamping one would erase who last
  moved the report and when — which is the only history this record keeps.
  Re-sending the same status is also not a change and does not re-stamp.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — empty body, unknown status, notes over 5,000 chars.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `platform:bugs:write`.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such report.
}
